meta {
  name: reject a person parenting a dog
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/archives/{{archiveId}}/relationships
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "parent",
    "fromSubjectId": "{{grandmotherId}}",
    "toSubjectId": "{{dogId}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("people and animals cannot share descendants", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(422);
    expect(res.body.error.details[0].code).to.equal("kind_mismatch");
  });
}

docs {
  Deliberately fails, and this is the constraint made structural: a parent
  edge requires both ends to be the same kind, so a shared descendant is not
  discouraged - it cannot be expressed.

  The affectionate version of this relationship still has a home; it is an
  `owner` edge.
}
